Keep rustc's export list on Windows GNU links

rustc writes a cdylib's exported symbols to a module definition file and
hands it to the linker as -Wl,<path>/list.def. cargo-zigbuild dropped it,
so lld exported every global symbol and could strip nothing. zig takes a
.def file as an input, so pass it that way instead. The last .def given
wins, so a crate that links its own replaces rustc's, as lld-link's /DEF
does on the MSVC targets.

